@startuml
!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #4A5568
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}

title Codex Development Workflow - Unified PR-Gated Lifecycle

state "Requirement" as requirement
state "Understand repo\nRead current state + architecture + relevant code\n[context-efficiency when context-heavy]" as understand
state "Plan\nScope / exclusions / acceptance / dependencies" as plan
state "Record Plan + Tickets + Slices\n[GitHub Issues before branch]\nOne feature -> one Plan;\nPlan contains one or more Tickets" as decompose
state "Create Plan feature branch\n(all change types)" as branch
state "Implement all Plan Tickets\n(main agent; optional bounded delegation)" as implement
state "Test + integrate Slices\n[test-workflow]\nminimal / focused / regression / full" as test
state "Staged redaction scan\nbefore commit\n[data-document-redaction]" as redact
state "Publication readiness + Commit\n[github-push-when-ready]\nIdentity / clean boundaries / Conventional Commits" as commit
state "Push branch\n[github-push-when-ready]" as push
state "Create / Update PR\n[github-push-when-ready]\nPR ready" as pr
state "pr-review\nSingle merge decision gate\nReturn PASS or BLOCKED" as review
state "Blocking findings?" as blocking #FFF4CC
state "Batch confirmed findings\nFix affected behavior" as fix
state "Test again\n[test-workflow]" as test_again
state "Redaction scan again\nafter review fix" as redact_again
state "Commit fix" as commit_fix
state "Push branch" as push_fix
state "Merge the Plan PR once\nRequired checks + PASS verified" as merge
state "Delete source branch" as delete_branch
state "Synchronize actual PR base\nFast-forward + prune" as update_main
state "Close Plan + child Tickets" as close_ticket
state "Update State / Docs\n[repo-current-state]" as state_docs
state "Deploy if needed\n[auto-deploy]" as deploy
state "Verify / Rollback" as verify #EAF2F8

[*] --> requirement
requirement --> understand
understand --> plan
plan --> decompose
decompose --> branch
branch --> implement
implement --> test
test --> redact
redact --> commit
commit --> push
push --> pr
pr --> review
review --> blocking
blocking --> fix : yes
blocking --> merge : no / pass
fix --> test_again
test_again --> redact_again
redact_again --> commit_fix
commit_fix --> push_fix
push_fix --> review : PR updated / review again
merge --> delete_branch
delete_branch --> update_main
update_main --> close_ticket
close_ticket --> state_docs
state_docs --> deploy : requested
state_docs --> [*] : not requested
deploy --> verify
verify --> [*] : pass
verify --> [*] : fail / rollback or escalate

note right of decompose
Persist one Plan Issue and all child Ticket Issues
before the Plan branch. The Plan owns one branch,
one PR, and one merge; all Tickets and Slices share it.
Ticket dependencies order work on that branch and
never create a Ticket-level merge.
Every feature has at least one Ticket; a small feature
uses one Ticket with one Slice.
end note

note right of review
Invoke immediately after the PR is ready.
Only PASS permits merge. BLOCKED returns to
Fix -> Test -> Redaction when applicable ->
Commit -> Push -> pr-review.
Review execution recovery is an implementation detail.
end note

note right of implement
Main agent owns integration and final judgment.
Delegate only independent, bounded work.
No overlapping files or shared interfaces in parallel.
Wrong design assumption -> re-plan.
Failed validation -> fix and rerun affected checks.
More Slices -> repeat implementation and validation.
  Publication waits for the whole Plan's acceptance.
Unresolved failures stop delivery.
end note

note right of push
Verify actual push URL(s) and destination branch.
Unknown targets and default-branch publication block.
All file types require a PR; never direct-push main.
end note

note right of state_docs
Update the recovery snapshot only after merge,
source-branch deletion, and default-branch sync.
If tracked State / Docs change, use the same
feature-branch and PR gate for that follow-up change.
end note

note left of requirement
Docs, Code, Tests, Config, Refactor, Bugfix,
Feature, Dependency, and CI/CD changes all use
this lifecycle. No direct default-branch delivery.
end note

@enduml
